## Backend and integrations

| Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|
| `GET /api/availability` | Bookable dates; with `?date=YYYY-MM-DD` it returns the open slots for that day |
| `POST /api/booking` | Validates the booking (zod) and re-checks that the slot is still free (409 if not). It then saves the booking, emails the company and the customer, creates a calendar event and forwards to the webhook |
| `POST /api/contact` | Contact form: saves the message and emails both sides |
| `POST /api/newsletter` | Newsletter signup. Connect your email service provider in this handler |

All endpoints have a **honeypot** field and **rate limiting**. The server adapters live in `src/services/server/`:

- **Email** (`email.ts`): Resend REST API. Swap in Postmark, SendGrid or SES without touching the routes.
- **Storage** (`storage.ts`): writes to a local file in development. **For production, replace `persist()` and `getBookedSlots()` with a database** such as Postgres, Supabase or Airtable.
- **Calendar** (`calendar.ts`): Google Calendar and Calendly integration points.
- **Rate limit** (`rate-limit.ts`): in-memory. Use Upstash Redis or similar when running multiple instances.

---

## Theming, motion and effects

- **Themes:** light by default, with dark available via the toggle. Colors are tokens in `src/app/globals.css`. Use the `theme-dark` class to keep a section dark in both themes.
- **Effects** in `src/components/effects/`: Lenis smooth scroll, a Canvas 2D particle field, a custom arrow-and-hand cursor, scroll-linked section fades, a shared observer for reveals, a scroll progress bar, back-to-top, a footer wordmark spotlight and a cookie notice.
- **Above-the-fold entrances** use CSS (`Enter`, `EnterText`), so they start on first paint.
- **Reduced motion:** every effect is disabled or made static when the visitor prefers reduced motion. The custom cursor only appears on mouse and trackpad devices.

## SEO

Every page has a unique title, description, canonical URL, Open Graph and X/Twitter tags (`buildMetadata()` in `src/lib/seo.ts`). Structured data is included for Organization, WebSite, ProfessionalService (LocalBusiness), Service, FAQPage, BlogPosting, BreadcrumbList and CreativeWork. `sitemap.xml`, `robots.txt`, a web manifest and OG images are generated automatically.

## Performance and accessibility

- **Static rendering:** every page is static (SSG). API routes are the only dynamic code.
- **3D hero:** loaded only on screens 768 px and wider, once the browser is idle. It pauses off-screen, and phones get a lightweight CSS orb instead.
- **Images:** served by `next/image` as AVIF/WebP at responsive sizes, with blur placeholders and lazy loading.
- **Videos:** muted, lazy-loaded and paused off-screen. They don't autoplay when reduced motion is on.
- **Scroll reveals:** server components driven by a single IntersectionObserver, so they add almost no hydration cost.
- **Accessibility:** skip link, semantic landmarks, logical heading order, labelled forms with inline errors, keyboard-accessible menus, a focus-trapped modal, visible focus rings and AA-contrast text tokens.

## Media credits

- **Photos:** [Unsplash](https://unsplash.com/license), free for commercial use. Source IDs are listed in `src/data/media.ts`.
- **Videos:** [Mixkit](https://mixkit.co/license/#videoFree), free commercial license.
- **Icons:** [Lucide](https://lucide.dev).

