## Quick start (run locally)

**Prerequisites:** [Node.js](https://nodejs.org) **20.9 or newer** (22 LTS recommended) and npm.

```bash
# 1. Clone
git clone https://github.com/mohakamran/nexvora-digital.git
cd nexvora-digital

# 2. Install dependencies
npm install

# 3. (Optional) configure environment variables. Everything works without them locally.
cp .env.example .env.local

# 4. Start the dev server
npm run dev
```

Open **http://localhost:3000**.

In development:
- Form submissions are saved to `.data/*.jsonl`, which git ignores.
- Emails are printed to the terminal instead of being sent, unless `RESEND_API_KEY` is set.

### Scripts

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `npm run dev` | Start the development server with hot reload |
| `npm run build` | Create an optimized production build |
| `npm start` | Serve the production build (run `build` first) |
| `npm run typecheck` | Type-check the project with TypeScript |

---

## Deploy to Vercel

1. Push this repository to GitHub (already done if you're reading this there).
2. Go to **[vercel.com/new](https://vercel.com/new)**, choose **Import Git Repository**, and select `nexvora-digital`.
3. Vercel detects **Next.js** automatically, so keep the defaults. The build command is `next build` and no output directory is needed.
4. Under **Environment Variables**, add the values you need (see the table below). At minimum, set `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` to your final domain.
5. Click **Deploy**. Every push to `main` redeploys automatically, and pull requests get preview URLs.
6. Optional:
   - Add your custom domain under **Settings → Domains**.
   - Enable **Analytics** and **Speed Insights** in the Vercel dashboard. They're already wired in, cookieless, and only load on Vercel.

> `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` is used for canonical URLs, the sitemap and Open Graph tags. If it isn't set, the site falls back to Vercel's production domain automatically.

---

## Environment variables

Copy `.env.example` to `.env.local` locally, or add the variables in your Vercel project settings. Only variables prefixed with `NEXT_PUBLIC_` reach the browser. Everything else stays server-side.

| Variable | Required | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` | Recommended | Public URL, e.g. `https://www.nexvora.com` |
| `RESEND_API_KEY` | For real email | [Resend](https://resend.com) API key for booking and contact emails |
| `EMAIL_FROM` | With Resend | Sender, e.g. `Nexvora Digital <info@nexvora.com>` (the domain must be verified in Resend) |
| `COMPANY_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL` | Optional | Inbox that receives new bookings and messages (default `info@nexvora.com`) |
| `LEADS_WEBHOOK_URL` | Optional | Forward every lead to a CRM, Zapier, Make, n8n or your own backend |
| `LEADS_WEBHOOK_SECRET` | Optional | HMAC-SHA256 signature sent in the `X-Signature` header |
| `GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID`, `GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON`, `CALENDLY_API_TOKEN` | Optional | Calendar integration (see `src/services/server/calendar.ts`) |

